-- title:
--   The stabilizer and the second logical qubit commute with $H$
-- statement:
--   Let $H$ be the four-qubit Hamiltonian (15.7), $S_1 = \sigma_x^{\otimes 4}$ and $S_2 = \sigma_z^{\otimes 4}$ the stabilizer generators of the $[4,2,2]$ code (15.5), and $\bar X_2 = I\otimes\sigma_x\otimes\sigma_x\otimes I$, $\bar Z_2 = \sigma_z\otimes\sigma_z\otimes I\otimes I$ the logical operators of the second encoded qubit (15.6). Then
--
--   $$[S_1, H] = [S_2, H] = [\bar Z_2, H] = [\bar X_2, H] = 0 .$$
--
--   Hence $H$ preserves each stabilizer sector and acts only on the first encoded qubit.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: the stabilizer of the [4,2,2] code → its generators S₁, S₂; reason: an operator commutes with the group generated by S₁, S₂ iff it commutes with S₁ and S₂
--   - encoding: qubits 1–4 → Lean qubits 0–3 (Pauli strings over `Fin 4`); reason: index base only
-- source:
--   Bacon, Decoherence, Control, and Symmetry in Quantum Computers, arXiv:quant-ph/0305025v1, §15.2, p.169 (PDF p.186)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_QMaxCutSDP_Rounding_Pauli
import Definitions.Def_BaconThesis_Supercoherence_S1
import Definitions.Def_BaconThesis_Supercoherence_S2
import Definitions.Def_BaconThesis_Supercoherence_X2bar
import Definitions.Def_BaconThesis_Supercoherence_Z2bar
import Definitions.Def_BaconThesis_Supercoherence_codeHamiltonian

open QMaxCutSDP.Rounding Matrix

namespace BaconThesis.Supercoherence

/-- Bacon, *Decoherence, Control, and Symmetry in Quantum Computers*, arXiv:quant-ph/0305025v1, §15.2, p.169 (PDF p.186): "The stabilizer of the [4, 2, 2] code commutes with this
Hamiltonian. Z̄2 and X̄2 also both commute with this Hamiltonian." The Hamiltonian `H` of (15.7)
commutes with the stabilizer generators `S₁, S₂` of (15.5) and with the logical operators `Z̄₂, X̄₂`
of (15.6).

**Formalization Note.** Four qubits, register `(Fin 4 → Fin 2) → ℂ`; Pauli strings via `QMaxCutSDP.Rounding.pauliString` (`pauli 0,1,2,3 = I, σ_x, σ_y, σ_z`); the book's qubit `k` is Lean's qubit `k - 1`. The stabilizer is generated by `S₁, S₂`, so commuting with the generators is commuting
with the stabilizer. -/
theorem commute_codeHamiltonian :
    Commute S1 codeHamiltonian ∧ Commute S2 codeHamiltonian ∧ Commute Z2bar codeHamiltonian ∧
      Commute X2bar codeHamiltonian := by sorry

end BaconThesis.Supercoherence
